1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,372
The Word Remains

2
00:00:03,372 --> 00:00:30,296
Sunday, four in the afternoon, the hour he would have taught. The university had stopped classes on the third day of the war. Professor Azad Moradi came anyway. Sixty empty chairs. Last semester’s chalk was still on the board: panta rhei, everything flows. He began to lecture to the empty chairs. “Can a just man live in an unjust state? That is today’s subject.”

3
00:00:30,896 --> 00:01:00,676
“Socrates drank the hemlock. But the dialogues remained.” On the board he wrote: logos menei, the word remains. From the doorway the custodian asked, “Will you teach next week too?” “I will.” That evening in Seoul, Kang Yujin sat before a model that had missed two Indian ships. It knew warships and missiles. Not phone calls between foreign ministers. She added one variable. Negotiation.

4
00:01:01,276 --> 00:01:05,064
Epic Fury continues in Episode 6.
